    <item>
      <title>Trump Headlines Texas Convention to Tap Donors, Rally Voters</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-09-09/trump-headlines-texas-convention-to-rally-donors-voters-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">53a1f29028b058361521509c</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 14:33:16 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>The two-day midterm political convention in Dallas this week is Republicans’ last, best chance to put on a show and appeal to donors and corporations ahead of a November election that’s increasingly favoring Democrats.

President Trump floated the idea of the convention a year ago as a way to rally voters and ensure Republican control of Congress. But it may be too late for that, given his flagging popularity and a second-term agenda that has failed to address voters’ economic concerns. For more, we speak with Julie Fine, Bloomberg News Texas Bureau Chief. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
